{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "EZK",
  "chapter": 42,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "EZK.42.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.42.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then he brought me forth into the outer court, the way towards the north: and he brought me into the chamber that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " over against the separate place, and which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " before the building towards the north.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.42.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.42.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Before the length of a hundred cubits ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the north door, and the breadth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fifty cubits.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.42.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.42.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Over against the twenty ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "cubits",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for the inner court, and over against the pavement which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for the outer court, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " gallery against gallery in three ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "stories",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.42.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.42.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And before the chambers ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a walk of ten cubits breadth inward, a way of one cubit; and their doors towards the north.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.42.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.42.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now the upper chambers ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " shorter: for the galleries were higher than these, than the lower, and than the middlemost of the building.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.42.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.42.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in three ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "stories",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", but had not pillars as the pillars of the courts: therefore ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the building",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " was straitened more than the lowest and the middlemost from the ground.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.42.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.42.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the wall that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " without over against the chambers, towards the outer court on the forepart of the chambers, the length of it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fifty cubits.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.42.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.42.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the length of the chambers that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the outer court ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fifty cubits: and lo, before the temple ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a hundred cubits.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.42.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.42.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And from under these chambers ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the entry on the east side, as one goeth into them from the outer court.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.42.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.42.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The chambers ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the thickness of the wall of the court towards the east, over against the separate place, and over against the building.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.42.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.42.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the way before them ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " like the appearance of the chambers which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " towards the north, as long as they, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as broad as they: and all their goings out ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " both according to their fashions, and according to their doors.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.42.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.42.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And according to the doors of the chambers that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " towards the south ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a door in the head of the way, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the way directly before the wall towards the east, as one entereth into them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.42.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.42.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then said he to me, The north chambers ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the south chambers which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " before the separate place, they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " holy chambers, where the priests that approach to the LORD shall eat the most holy things: there shall they lay the most holy things, and the meat-offering, and the sin-offering, and the trespass-offering; for the place ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " holy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.42.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.42.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When the priests enter therein, then shall they not go out of the holy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "place",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " into the outer court, but there they shall lay their garments in which they minister; for they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " holy; and shall put on other garments, and shall approach to ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "those things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for the people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.42.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.42.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now when he had made an end of measuring the inner house, he brought me forth towards the gate whose prospect ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " towards the east, and measured it around.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.42.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.42.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He measured the east side with the measuring reed, five hundred reeds, with the measuring reed around.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.42.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.42.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He measured the north side, five hundred reeds, with the measuring reed around.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.42.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.42.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He measured the south side, five hundred reeds, with the measuring reed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.42.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.42.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He turned about to the west side, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " measured five hundred reeds, with the measuring reed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.42.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.42.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He measured it by the four sides: it had a wall around, five hundred ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "reeds",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " long, and five hundred broad, to make a separation between the sanctuary and the profane place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
